From 8217e9d8f1113f4b4d0f451200043128529c4f7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SlateX Pipeline <pipeline@slatex.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 05:03:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix $project token in Artists/Projects grandchild
 sequence.yml files

Live folder creation still failed after the prior fix (5306bef), with
the identical error moved one level deeper:

  tank.errors.TankError: Error resolving filter expression
  [{'path': 'project', 'relation': 'is', 'values': ['$project']}] in
  .../core/schema/Artists/sg_projectcode/sequence.yml: The
  configuration expression $project could not be found in  or in any
  of its parents.

5306bef correctly fixed sg_projectcode.yml itself (the direct child of
the new Artists/Projects project-type roots) but missed that
sequence.yml, ONE LEVEL DEEPER under it, has the exact same problem for
the exact same reason: tk-core's $token resolution walks up the schema
tree matching against an ancestor folder's LITERAL NAME. There is no
folder literally named 'project' above sequence.yml either (only
'Artists' -> 'sg_projectcode' -> 'sequence'), so $project fails there
too, regardless of sg_projectcode.yml's own token already being fixed.

Fix: same pattern as 5306bef - $project -> $Artists in
core/schema/Artists/sg_projectcode/sequence.yml, and $project ->
$Projects in core/schema/Projects/sg_projectcode/Plates/sequence.yml.
Verified via full grep sweep that no other $project reference remains
anywhere in either schema tree, at any depth (shot.yml one level
further down uses $sequence, referencing its own immediate parent
folder - a different, already-correctly-scoped token, not $project).

Also strengthened tests/test_schema_token_resolution.py: the previous
version's static check
(test_schema_files_use_fixed_token_not_project) was accidentally gated
behind the same module-level tk-core-availability skipif as the
tk-core-dependent tests, even though it needs no tk-core at all - so it
never actually ran and could not have caught this regression despite
being designed to guard against exactly this. Replaced with
test_no_project_token_anywhere_in_artists_or_projects_trees, which (a)
always runs regardless of environment, and (b) globs every .yml file
under core/schema/Artists/ and core/schema/Projects/ at any depth,
instead of checking a fixed list of two file paths - so a third
occurrence at a still-deeper level in the future can't slip through
undetected the way this one did. Also added a new tk-core-backed test,
test_grandchild_can_still_reach_artists_token, exercising real
FilterExpressionToken resolution two levels below the Artists root
(the actual depth this bug occurred at), not just one level as the
previous version tested.

Full existing test suite (tests/test_templates.py, tests/
test_schema_token_resolution.py) passes: 11 passed, 5 skipped (skipped
tests need a real tk-core checkout, unavailable in this environment -
same limitation as before, unchanged by this fix).
